---
/**
 * Why Our Bottles Have Vented Caps — /vented-caps/
 *
 * Support page linked from the Order Delivered email. It answers one question:
 * "there's liquid around the cap, did I get ripped off?" Reassurance first,
 * explanation second, escalation path last.
 *
 * Migrated from the Shopify page at shop.southlandorganics.com/pages/vented-caps,
 * which was never ported. middleware.ts sent /pages/vented-caps -> /contact/, so
 * every customer clicking the link in a delivery email landed on a contact form
 * instead of the answer.
 *
 * 🛑 TWO CLAIMS FROM THE SHOPIFY ORIGINAL WERE CORRECTED, NOT COPIED:
 *
 * 1. "they release small amounts of METHANE" — dropped. Our own product content
 *    names *Bacillus* strains, which are facultative aerobes: they produce CO2,
 *    not methane. Methanogens are strict anaerobic archaea and are not what is in
 *    a probiotic bottle. Every other methane reference in our content is about
 *    septic/anaerobic digestion, a different process. Now reads "a small amount
 *    of gas" — true without naming a compound we cannot support.
 *
 * 2. "OUR liquid products are packed with beneficial microbes" — too broad.
 *    Peracetic acid is an antimicrobial oxidizer; D2 sanitizers are not probiotic.
 *    Now reads "many of our liquid products."
 *
 * If someone can source the methane claim from a lab result, put it back. Until
 * then this is the version that cannot be shown to be wrong in public.
 */

export const prerender = true

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/shared/Breadcrumbs.astro'
import { getCloudinaryResponsiveSet, getSouthlandImageId } from '../lib/cloudinary'

const siteUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL || 'https://southlandorganics.com'

const hero = getCloudinaryResponsiveSet(
  getSouthlandImageId('heroes/Farm_Athens_GA_7_jbdjik'),
  [800, 1200, 1600, 1920],
  { crop: 'fill', quality: 'auto', format: 'auto', effect: ['saturation:60', 'brightness:80'] }
)

const title = 'Why Our Bottles Have Vented Caps | Southland Organics'
const description =
  "Notice a little liquid around the cap? Nothing's wrong, and you didn't lose any of what you paid for. Here's why our bottles vent."

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Why do Southland Organics bottles have vented caps?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Many of our liquid products are alive. The beneficial microbes in them keep working after the bottle is filled, and as they do they release a small amount of gas. A sealed cap would trap it and the bottle would swell, then split. The vent lets it out.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Why did some liquid leak out of my bottle during shipping?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "When pressure escapes, a bit of liquid can come with it, especially after a bottle has been jostled in a truck. We overfill every bottle to account for it, so the full labeled amount is there.",
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Is the product still good if it vented?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Yes. A little venting means the biology is active, which is exactly what you are paying for.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can I replace the vented cap with a solid one?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'No. Sealing the bottle is what makes it burst. Check the cap is seated snugly instead — it will still vent, and that is fine.',
      },
    },
  ],
}
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalUrl={`${siteUrl}/vented-caps/`}
  schema={schema}
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <img
      src={hero.src}
      srcset={hero.srcset}
      sizes="100vw"
      alt="Southland Organics farm in Athens, Georgia"
      class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
      width="1600"
      height="1067"
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#2C5234]/85"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
      <p
        class="font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-green-300"
        style="font-size:0.8125rem;"
      >
        Product care
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-heading mt-3 text-4xl uppercase text-white md:text-5xl">
        Why Our Bottles Have Vented Caps
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-green-100">
        Notice a little liquid around the cap? Nothing&rsquo;s wrong, and you didn&rsquo;t lose
        any of what you paid for. Here&rsquo;s why.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Why Our Bottles Have Vented Caps', href: '/vented-caps/' },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- Body -->
  <section class="bg-white py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl uppercase text-[#2C5234] md:text-3xl">
        The cap is doing a job
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#191D21]">
        Many of our liquid products are alive. The beneficial microbes in them keep working
        after the bottle is filled, and as they do, they release a small amount of gas. A sealed
        cap would trap it &mdash; the bottle would swell, then split. The vent lets it out.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-heading mt-12 text-2xl uppercase text-[#2C5234] md:text-3xl">
        If a little leaked out, nothing is wrong
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#191D21]">
        When pressure escapes, a bit of liquid can come with it, especially after a bottle has
        been jostled in a truck. <strong>We overfill every bottle to account for it.</strong> The
        full labeled amount is there.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-heading mt-12 text-2xl uppercase text-[#2C5234] md:text-3xl">
        Is the product still good?
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#191D21]">
        Yes. A little venting means the biology is active &mdash; which is exactly what
        you&rsquo;re paying for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Storage -->
  <section class="bg-[#F8FAF8] py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl uppercase text-[#2C5234] md:text-3xl">
        When your order arrives
      </h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 list-none space-y-3 pl-0">
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#191D21]">
          <span class="mt-1 font-bold text-[#44883E]" aria-hidden="true">&check;</span>
          <span>Wipe off the bottle</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#191D21]">
          <span class="mt-1 font-bold text-[#44883E]" aria-hidden="true">&check;</span>
          <span>
            Check the cap is seated snugly &mdash; it&rsquo;ll still vent, and that&rsquo;s fine
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#191D21]">
          <span class="mt-1 font-bold text-[#44883E]" aria-hidden="true">&check;</span>
          <span>Store it upright, cool and dry, out of reach of children and pets</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#191D21]">
          <span class="mt-1 font-bold text-[#44883E]" aria-hidden="true">&check;</span>
          <span>
            Don&rsquo;t swap in a solid cap &mdash; sealing the bottle is what makes it burst
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Help -->
  <section class="bg-[#2C5234] py-14 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl uppercase text-white md:text-3xl">More than a little?</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-green-100">
        If a bottle showed up visibly low, cracked, or soaked through the box, that&rsquo;s not
        normal venting. Send us a photo and we&rsquo;ll make it right.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-7">
        <a
          href="mailto:success@southlandorganics.com"
          class="inline-block rounded-lg bg-[#44883E] px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold text-white no-underline"
        >
          Email success@southlandorganics.com
        </a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-green-200">
        Or call <a href="tel:18006083755" class="text-white underline">800-608-3755</a> &mdash; a
        real person answers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
